---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Notice from "../components/Notice.astro";
import { ads, site } from "../config";

const minutesBetween = ads.secondsBetweenInterstitials / 60;

const description = `Advertising policy for ${site.name}. Optional rewarded ads, interstitials between runs, and Remove Ads.`;
---

<Base title="Advertising Policy" description={description}>
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="kicker">Advertising Policy</p>
    <h1>Advertising Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {site.updated}</p>
    <Notice />
    <p>
      {site.name} is free to start. A store build may include advertising to support the game. This
      page explains what those ads are, when they can appear, and how to limit them. Questions go
      to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Who serves the ads</h2>
    <p>
      Ads are served by Google AdMob. Google's privacy policy applies to the ad request:
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      We do not sell ad space ourselves. Advertisers do not get a game account from you, because
      the game does not have accounts.
    </p>

    <h2>Rewarded ads</h2>
    <p>
      Some ads are optional. You choose to watch one. A completed rewarded ad can grant energy, or
      continue a run in Endless Voyage. Closing it early does not grant the reward. The game does
      not require a rewarded ad in order to play.
    </p>

    <h2>Interstitial ads</h2>
    <p>
      An interstitial is a full-screen ad between runs. It is not shown while you are aiming, and
      it is not shown while Spark is in flight.
    </p>
    <p>
      The game waits until you have finished at least {ads.runsBeforeFirstInterstitial} runs before
      the first interstitial. After that, at least {ads.runsBetweenInterstitials} runs and {minutesBetween}
      minutes pass between interstitials. If you just watched a rewarded ad, the next interstitial
      is held back.
    </p>

    <h2>Remove Ads</h2>
    <p>
      The in-app purchase named Remove Ads stops forced interstitial ads. It does not remove the
      choice to watch a rewarded ad, including a continue you start yourself in Endless Voyage.
      The store product id is {site.removeAdsProductId}. Apple or Google handles the payment, as
      described in the <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What an ad can know</h2>
    <p>
      When ads are enabled, AdMob may use an advertising identifier, coarse device information such
      as language and general device type, the app id, and whether an ad was shown or tapped.
      Google may process an IP address to deliver the ad and to limit fraud. We do not keep a copy
      of your advertising identifier.
    </p>
    <p>
      If the app asks for permission to track you across apps and websites owned by other
      companies, you can refuse. You can also reset or delete the advertising identifier, and opt
      out of ads personalization, in your phone's settings. Those choices can limit personalized
      ads. They do not have to turn ads off entirely.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The game is not directed at children under 13. Ad requests are not made as child-directed
      treatment. We do not use ads to build a profile of a child.
    </p>

    <h2>Test builds</h2>
    <p>
      Some test builds have advertising switched off. The rules on this page apply to a store
      build in which advertising is enabled.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {site.publisher}<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
